---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Japan Living Edit, an independent English-language editorial website covering Japanese living ideas for international readers."
  pathname="/about/"
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>An independent editorial view on everyday living from Japan.</h1>
    <p>
      Japan Living Edit is a Japan-based independent editorial website publishing
      English-language content for international readers, with a primary focus on
      readers in the United States.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="text-block">
    <p>
      The site covers thoughtfully designed products and everyday living ideas from
      Japan across the home, kitchen, table, coffee, organization and other areas of
      daily life. It is not an official website for any brand, retailer or affiliate
      program.
    </p>
    <p>
      The editorial goal is simple: explain what makes certain objects, routines and
      home ideas useful in real daily life by looking at function, materials,
      construction, design details and everyday usefulness.
    </p>
    <h2>Editorial approach</h2>
    <p>
      Coverage is chosen editorially, with attention to thoughtful function,
      materials and construction, practical design details and the relationship
      between form and everyday use. Manufacturer specifications, materials and
      production information can help explain reliability, but we do not guarantee
      long-term durability for products we have not used or inspected closely.
    </p>
    <p>
      Japan Living Edit looks for specific details that matter: a shape that solves a
      task, a material that affects care, a construction choice that can be verified,
      or a visual design decision that supports how an object is used.
    </p>
    <h2>Editorial independence</h2>
    <p>
      Inclusion on the site does not imply sponsorship, endorsement or an official
      relationship. Future commercial relationships should be disclosed clearly, and
      products should not receive positive coverage simply because an affiliate
      relationship exists.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some articles may be explanatory guides or editorial notes rather than hands-on
      reviews. When a product has not been personally tested, the article should avoid
      presenting it as a tested recommendation.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
